Date: Wed, 17 Jun 2026 03:46:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02246/11362] [outer-loop] relicense project Apache-2.0 ->
 MIT-0 (sole-author decision; ARC Prize prize-eligibility)

Operator decision (AskUserQuestion 2026-06-17): whole-project MIT-0 for foolproof ARC
Prize 2026 eligibility ('submitter-authored solution code must be CC0/MIT-0'). Sole
author, so relicensable without consent issues.

Legally-operative:
- LICENSE -> MIT No Attribution (+ third-party carve-out note)
- NOTICE -> Carnot code is MIT-0; PRESERVES the THRML Apache-2.0 third-party attribution
- pyproject.toml license = MIT-0, classifier MIT, license-files keeps NOTICE
Forward-looking generators -> MIT-0: hf_publisher model-card template, session_memory_pack
DEFAULT_LICENSE, carnot_ebm_modelcard_v53. Public: README frontmatter (license: other +
license_name mit-0), docs/index.html badge/meta, CLAUDE.md project vision. Code+test:
phase1_ship_readiness now asserts MIT-0 (test fixture updated; 6/6 green).

PRESERVED as Apache-2.0 (third-party, MUST NOT relicense): python/carnot/sampling/
_vendored_thrml/, python/carnot/phase3/ebt_upstream/, and references to third-party
licenses (D-Wave Ocean SDK, gpt-oss teacher). LEFT per never-prune: historical
experiment_NNN scripts whose artifacts recorded Apache-2.0 at the time (their tests pin
that historical output). HF license tag uses 'other'+mit-0 (HF has no mit-0 tag).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
